WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.890
24 May 2013.

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.030
Under the Okhotsk Sea,
an earthquake strikes.

3
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.690
Its magnitude: 8.3.

4
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:13.570
It was felt all over Asia: in
Tokyo, and as far away as Moscow.

5
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.070
Yet a quake that big can do less
damage than others of the same size.

6
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:19.070
How?

7
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.070
Was it smaller than it seemed?

8
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.850
In this mission, you'll see why
earthquakes happen where plates lock,

9
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.130
and where in the world they strike.

10
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.830
Then you'll compare the
four types of plate margin,

11
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.470
and the earthquakes each one makes.

12
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:37.390
Your mission: explain why a quake that
big can do less damage than others of the

13
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.430
same size.
